{"path":"types/numeric_limits/traps","title":"std::numeric_limits<T>::traps","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::numeric_limits&lt;T&gt;::</span>traps","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/traps","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"The value of std::numeric_limits<T>::traps is true for all arithmetic types T that have at least one value at the start of the program that, if used as an argument to an arithmetic operation, will generate a trap.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev\">\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> traps<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> traps<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> for all arithmetic types <code>T</code> that have at least one value at the start of the program that, if used as an argument to an arithmetic operation, will generate a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trap_(computing)\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">trap</a>. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Standard_specializations\">Standard specializations</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td>  <code>T</code>\n</td>\n<td>  value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/* non-specialized */</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">signed</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">wchar_t</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">char8_t</span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char16_t</span></span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char32_t</span></span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">short</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">short</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">float</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>  usually <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>On most platforms integer division by zero always traps, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> for all integer types that support the value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>. The exception is the type <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>: even though division by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> traps due to integral promotion from <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span> to <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>, it is the zero-valued <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span> that traps. Zero is not a value of type <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>.\n</p><p>On most platforms, floating-point exceptions may be turned on and off at run time (e.g. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">feenableexcept<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on Linux or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">_controlfp</span></code> on Windows), in which case the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span></span></code> for floating-point types reflects the state of floating-point trapping facility at the time of program startup, which is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> on most modern systems. An exception would be a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DEC_Alpha\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">DEC Alpha</a> program, where it is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> if compiled without <code>-ieee</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;limits&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/boolalpha\"><span class=\"kw1780\">std::<span class=\"me2\">boolalpha</span></span></a>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"bool:     traps = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"char:     traps = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"char16_t: traps = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">char16_t</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"long:     traps = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">long</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"float:    traps = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">float</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">traps</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>// GCC output:\nbool:     traps = true\nchar:     traps = true\nchar16_t: traps = true\nlong:     traps = true\nfloat:    traps = false\n&nbsp;\n// Clang output:\nbool:     traps = false\nchar:     traps = true\nchar16_t: traps = true\nlong:     traps = true\nfloat:    traps = false</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue497\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 497</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>it was unclear what is returned if trapping<br>is enabled or disabled at runtime\n</td>\n<td>returns the enable status<br>at the start of the program\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv\">Floating-point environment</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/tinyness_before\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>tinyness_before</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  identifies floating-point types that detect tinyness before rounding <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member constant)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/has_denorm_loss\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>has_denorm_loss</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  identifies the floating-point types that detect loss of precision as denormalization loss rather than inexact result <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member constant)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Standard specializations","id":"Standard_specializations"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"},{"path":"types/numeric_limits","title":"std::numeric_limits"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::numeric_limits<T>::traps","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++11, since C++11. The value of std::numeric_limits<T>::traps is true for all arithmetic types T that have at least one…"},{"label":"Standard specializations","children":[{"label":"/* non-specialized */","note":"false"},{"label":"bool","note":"false"},{"label":"char","note":"usually true"},{"label":"signed char","note":"usually true"},{"label":"unsigned char","note":"usually true"},{"label":"wchar_t","note":"usually true"},{"label":"char8_t (since C++20)","note":"usually true"},{"label":"+13 more"}]},{"label":"Notes","note":"On most platforms integer division by zero always traps, and std::numeric_limits<T>::traps is true for all integer types that support the value 0 ."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"tinyness_before","note":"identifies floating-point types that detect tinyness before rounding"},{"label":"has_denorm_loss","note":"identifies the floating-point types that detect loss of precision as denormalization loss rather than inexact result"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":452,"codeBlockCount":2}
